From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:11:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 461/488] [DS4.1] Logit bias: the restore scan stops at the
 first live tile

The all-masked check reads the row a tile at a time; each tile now ends
with __syncthreads_or (one barrier that ORs the block's flags) and the
scan stops once a column is alive, since the answer cannot change. A
dead row still reads every column; the verdict is the same. Run 20's
gate measured the structured min-tokens case at 96 rows 1.1 us behind
Triton (inside the noise); a row with a live column now reads one tile.
A test puts the only live column in the first, a middle, the last whole
and the partial tile, and a NaN-only and a dead row, against Triton.
